					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harvoable" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005588); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7005588&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606400356" alt="Harvoable " style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7005588)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harvoable" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005588); return false;" >Harvoable </a></span> <span class="odate time_1606396496 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Nov 2020 13:14</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828533">
									

<p>No worries; keep in mind I'm not an official critter, so take what I said with a grain of salt. Regarding the similarity to God of War, it's not necessarily a bad thing if you can put your own spin on it (and it's well written). Regarding the Mary-Sue comment, I was referring to the fact that the entity is near-indestructible; there's already a lot of articles like that on the site, so it comes across a little cliché. Just an idea, but maybe he was much stronger in his original dimension, but in the ours, he's less formidable? But again, this is all just my opinion; if you can pull off a near-indestructible demigod, go for it!</p>
<p>I'm not sure if you know, but posters are typically expected to contact seasoned critters from <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/butterfly-squad-roster">The Butterfly Squad</a> for feedback. So look through the list, see who'd be most suited to give you feedback, and send off a couple of WikiDot PMs. Alternatively, you can contact people in the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/chat-guide">IRC Chat</a>. If you don't contact anyone, you might be waiting a while before someone authorised to give greenlights will come along.</p>
<p>Good luck with your article!</p>

